  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Thundercat Technology has received $143M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Thundercat Technology won 29 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.9M. Thundercat Technology obligations fell 87.7% year over year. Thundercat Technology received $142M from the Department of Veterans Affairs in FY2027 to date. Thundercat Technology also received smaller obligations from the Department of Transportation, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, and the National Archives and Records Administration, and received no obligations from several major agencies listed for this period. Looking at recent fiscal years, Thundercat Technology obligations were $680M in FY22, $854M in FY23, $804M in FY24, $913M in FY25, and $1.2B in FY26, before the current-year total of $143M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers of Thundercat Technology this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the main buyer, obligating $142M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Transportation obligated $603K, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $216K, and the National Archives and Records Administration obligated $80.8K. Several major agencies recorded $0 in obligations for Thundercat Technology in this period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Thundercat Technology's federal business trended over recent years?",
        "body": "Thundercat Technology obligations rose from $680M in FY22 to $854M in FY23, then were $804M in FY24, $913M in FY25, and $1.2B in FY26. Thundercat Technology obligations are $143M in FY27 to date, a change described as down 87.7% year over year. Thundercat Technology received 29 awards in FY2027 to date with an average award size of $4.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
